# Evaluation of the fixed literal words

The long Sylow words are decomposed by list concatenation. The selected DAG
is then evaluated by multiplication and certified right inverses. This
proves the rows of the actual subgroup elements, not just candidate matrices.

Source: the literal ATLAS max1 kernel and Sylow words; see
`SylowNormalEights/source/README.md`. Generated by
`MatrixRealization/source/semantics.py`. Arithmetic uses only kernel-checked
row products, with the original basis and multiplication convention.
-/

